  set:  # d4ec
    title: "The '::' / colon-in-slot module-hint corruption moved: symbol_path_slot is FIXED, io_boundary._extract_module_hint still takes parts[1] and shreds rust 'std::fs' to 'std'"  # d4ec
    fields:  # d4ec
      root_cause: "RELOCATED 2026-08-09, mechanism still live but NOT where this item filed it.\n\nWHAT IS FIXED: ir.symbol_path_slot -- the function this item named -- is now\nRIGHT-ANCHORED per ADR-0036 D1a and its docstring says so explicitly. Verified:\nsymbol_path_slot('rust:std::fs:0-0:create_dir_all:unresolved') -> 'std::fs'.\nCorrect. It also self-documents that it exists as a chokepoint because the fact\npreviously had four homes, two of which took parts[1].\n\nWHAT IS STILL BROKEN: io_boundary._extract_module_hint does NOT route through\nthat chokepoint. It still does edge_dst.split(':') and takes parts[1]. Verified\non merged dev: _extract_module_hint('rust:std::fs:0-0:create_dir_all:unresolved')\n-> 'std'. The hint then fails _module_matches against the catalogue's 'std::fs'\nand the lookup returns None -- the REJECTING branch this item was filed about.\n\nSo the chokepoint consolidation happened and this caller was never migrated to\nit. Anyone 'fixing symbol_path_slot' again will find nothing to fix."  # d4ec
- op: discuss  # f9c5
  at: '2026-08-10T02:40:57Z'  # f9c5
  by: agent  # f9c5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f9c5
  clock: 5  # f9c5
  nonce: f9c5  # f9c5
  message: "MECHANISM RELOCATED, WITH EVIDENCE -- and found accidentally, which is worth\nrecording. 2026-08-09.\n\nWhile building the cross-language parity test for INV-sapit (PR #256), the RUST\narm failed: the real std::fs.create_dir_all call stopped matching the catalogue.\nThat was this defect reproducing independently, in a test written for something\nelse.\n\nMEASURED, side by side on merged dev:\n\n  dst = rust:std::fs:0-0:create_dir_all:unresolved\n    ir.symbol_path_slot(dst)             -> 'std::fs'   CORRECT (right-anchored)\n    io_boundary._extract_module_hint(dst) -> 'std'      CORRUPTED (parts[1])\n\nSo the fix this item asked for LANDED in symbol_path_slot and the io-boundary\ncaller was never migrated onto it. The item's own root_cause and title both\nstill point at the fixed function, which would send the next reader to code that\nis already correct.\n\nWHY IT IS PARTLY MASKED IN PRODUCTION, so the gap is not oversold: for an\nexternal target, production analyzers supply a structured dst_ref (WI-tihup) and\ntag_io_boundaries PREFERS it, bypassing the colon-split entirely. That is why a\nreal rust probe tags std::fs.create_dir_all correctly today while the synthetic\nedge does not. THE SIZE OF THE UNMASKED POPULATION -- boundary-relevant edges\nthat carry a '::' or otherwise colon-bearing module slot AND no dst_ref -- IS\nNOT MEASURED. Do not treat 'production mostly routes around it' as a closure\nargument; measure it.\n\nFIX SHAPE, when someone takes this: route _extract_module_hint through\nsymbol_path_slot rather than re-deriving the parse, which is the consolidation\nsymbol_path_slot's own docstring says it exists for. That is a chokepoint\nmigration, not a new predicate.\n\nStatus stays violated. Nothing here is closure evidence."  # f9c5
